I've always been a little disappointed that credit cards don't work in
shops. I've been thinking about how to fix this without breaking the
game, and I've come up with an idea: what if credit cards can be used
as "bags of holding" for gold. That is, you can effectively put gold
into the card and carry it around without any weight penalty.

Of course, it wouldn't be quite that simple. You can't just add and
remove gold from your card by #looting it. You'd need the help of a
shopkeeper. You could drop gold in a shop and then apply the card to
the shopkeeper to have it added to you credit. Each card would have a
credit limit (ie maximum capacity), (which could be based on its
enchantment), so you couldn't do the old pet-trick to get arbitrarily
large amounts of credit, but it would be useful for carrying small
amounts of credit from one shop to another.

When you found a card it could have a certain (unknown) amount of
credit on it, just like finding a pile of gold.

If you used a cursed credit card there would be a fair chance that the
shopkeeper noticed the signature was wrong and called the Kops.

Leprechauns could steal your credit cards as well as your cash.

This seems eminently easy to patch. I think I'll give it a go.

